# Keep the current session design
- Access token is a JWT, about 20 minutes. Refresh token is random, stored hashed, path /api/auth, about 7 days.
- Cookies are HttpOnly and SameSite=Strict. Secure is on only when COOKIE_SECURE=1.
- CSRF is the csrf_token cookie compared with X-CSRF-Token on state-changing requests.
- Decode with algorithms=["HS256"] and the key from CONSOLE_JWT_KEY_FILE. Never take alg from the token header.
- jti is revoked on logout and when the session version changes. Password change must keep that revocation.
- Unknown user and wrong password return the same error. The dummy Argon2 hash must stay so timing does not reveal the account.
- Idle timeout is only 5, 15, 30, or 60 minutes. Absolute lifetime is 12 hours from sign-in.
- First admin password is admin and must_change_password blocks the API until it is replaced. Do not bypass that gate.
- New passwords are at least 12 characters. Hash with argon2-cffi PasswordHasher. Never log or return the hash.
- Do not require iss or aud until both the issuer and the decoder set them. Adding only the check logs everyone out.
- X-Forwarded-For is trusted only when remote_addr is in TRUSTED_PROXIES. Use the right-most hop.
- Guest scans are a separate cookie. Do not treat a guest id as a user id.
